2 CONT
2 CONT '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/9HJ3-RKX
2 CONT Brief Life History of Victoire'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Victoire Tetreau was born on 30 May 1746, in Saint-Charles, Montreal, Quebec, British North America, her father, Jean Baptiste Tetreau dit Ducharme, was 31 and her mother, Marie Angelique Benoit Livernois, was 31. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Paul Brunel (1753-1766) on 27 February 1764, in Saint-Charles, Montreal, Quebec, British North America. No children.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 2nd husband Louis Racette (1746–1820)
2 CONT on 23 October 1769 in Saint-Charles-sur-Richelieu, Saint-Hyacinthe, Quebec, Canada
2 CONT They had at least 6 children:
2 CONT Marie Louise Racette 1770–1823
2 CONT Marie Charlotte Racette 1772–1854
2 CONT Louis Racette 1773–1822
2 CONT Marie Magdeleine Racette 1775–1823
2 CONT Charles Racette 1781–1781
2 CONT Joseph Racet 1782–
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 25 October 1809, in Saint-Hilaire, Bedford, Lower Canada, British North America, at the age of 63.
