1 NAME Jean John Baptiste /Beaudry/
2 GIVN Jean John Baptiste
2 _MARNM Beaudry
2 NICK Jean Baptiste Beaudry            March 25
2 NICK 1786 - March 03
2 NICK 1848
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 3 MAR 1848
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saint-Charles-sur-Richelieu
3 STAE Québec
3 CTRY Canada
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 MAR 1848
2 PLAC New Hague, Ticonderoga, New York, USA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~hagueny/delarm/family_jean_baptisite_beaudry.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Baptiste Beaudry            March 25, 1786 - March 03, 1848              (Jean Baptiste Beaudry + Marie Anne Tetreault dit Ducharme)
2 CONT     Marie Euphrosine Baille   January 11, 1794 - November 30, 1868     ( Pierre Baille dit Printemps + Marie Anne Dufault dit Raclos)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Baptiste (John)  Beaudry was born in St. Charles Sur Richelieu, Québec, Canada. Marie Euphrosine (Mary) was born in St. Matthias Sur Richelieu, Québec, Canada. Mary died in Benson, Rutland Co., VT while staying with her son, 
2 CONC Charles, and his family. They are buried in the McCaughin Cemetery on McDougal Dr. which is near the original location of the Catholic Church in Ticonderoga, NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Mary were married on September 17, 1811 in Ste Marie de Monnoir, Marieville, Québec, Canada. 
2 CONT                                                 (Sept. 17, 1811 part b)
2 CONT
2 CONT They ran a small bakery and restaurant while they lived near Marieville Québec. They did their best business during the apple harvest for their home was then crowded with apple buyers all day and all night long. The buyers loved t
2 CONC o gamble at cards, generally the game of Loo. Gambling went on all day and night on Sundays, except during religious services. Jean and Marie were prominent and devoted members of the Church. Jean and two sons, Charles and Louis, 
2 CONC served in the choir. (From the notes of Richard D. Wormwood - he indicates the source for this is The Spiritual Struggle of a Roman Catholic, by Louis N. Beaudry).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Beaudry family moved to Hague, Warren Co., NY before 1848 and lived there until after 1865.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Mary had 15 children
2 CONT
2 CONT http://gw.geneanet.org/famillearbour?lang=fr;p=elie;n=beaudry
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.isalpi.com/webtrees/individual.php?pid=I7497&ged=beaudry022011.ged
