1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baptism Record translation 
2 CONT
2 CONT This image is a hand-written baptismal record from a French-Canadian parish register, dated January 27, 1817. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     •    Subject: The record documents the baptism of Pierre Simion. 
2 CONT     •    Parents: He is the son of Charles Beauregard, a cultivator in the parish, and Élisabeth Bourque. 
2 CONT     •    Godparents: The godfather is Abraham Bourque and the godmother is Pauline Dufort. 
2 CONT     •    Signatures: The document is signed by a priest (identified in search results as J. B. Bédard) and notes the presence of the father. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation 
2 CONT     •    Date: The twenty-seventh of January one thousand eight hundred and seventeen, by us parish priest undersigned was baptized Pierre Simion, born the same day, legitimate son of the marriage of Charles Beauregard, cultivator
2 CONC  in this parish, and of Élisabeth Bourque. 
2 CONT     •    Godparents: The godfather was Abraham Bourque and the godmother Pauline Dufort, who have signed with us, as well as the father present. 
2 CONT     •    Signature: J. B. Bédard, priest.
