1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pioneer Dies In 92nd Year
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Richard M. Stewart, a member of one of the pioneer families of Rolph township, died Sunday in hospital here after an illness of three months. She would, had she lived, observed her 92nd birthday on May 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Stewart, the former Annie Laurie Meilleur, was born in Rolph township, a daughter of the late Mr. and Mrs. Joseph Meilleur, who were among the earliest residents of that area. Many years ago she married Richard Martin Stewart,
2 CONC  a native of Sand Point, and lived most of her life in Rolph. She later lived for eight years in Pembroke and for the past year, until entering hospital, lived at Deux Rivieres with her daughter, Mrs. Andrew Cotnam.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband died 27 years ago and she is survived by four sons, Wallace, Pembroke ; Archie, Sudbury ; Richard, Port Hope, and James, London, Ont., and four daughters, Mrs. A. Cotnam, Deux Rivieres ; Mrs. R. Larochelle, Rolphton ; 
2 CONC Mrs. Alex. MacDonald, Pembroke, and Mrs. E. Miller, Copper Cliff, while there are three brothers, Hector, Des-Joachims ; Gus, Mackey, and John, Rolph, and three sisters, Mrs. Paul Poirier, Pembroke ; Mrs. Ben Lance and Mrs. Ben Du
2 CONC foe, Point Alexander.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are also 30 grandchildren, 23 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral will be held Tuesday morning, with burial in the Stewart plot in Sand Point cemetery.
