2 CONT Mr. Frank Ash, aged 71 yrs passed peacefully away onTuesdayevening,July 25th at his home in Clinton, NY., near ClintonMills.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Ash was born in Canada and while but a small boy, movedwithhisparents to Charolett, Vt., where he remained until 1865 whenhemovedto Clinton, NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was united in marriage to miss Rachel Hall and to thisuniononechild was born, and after the Death of his first wifewasagainmarried to Miss Mary Oldham and to this union nine childrenwereborn,one dying while yet Young.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased had for some time before his Death complainedofhearttrouble, but the end was not looked for and his Death came asashockto his many friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a man of courage and perseverance being able toendurethehardships which fall to the lot of the first settlers of whatiscallthe woods.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by six daughters and three sons:  IdaM.Hill,Montpelier, Vt..:  Lusetta Leggett, Washington, Vt., VinaM.Sinton,Berline, Vt.: Betres Knapper, Regina, Manitoba:  Henry,Bisbee,Arizona:  John, George and Mary, who live a
2 CONC t the oldhomestead. Hiswife having died in 1887.
2 CONT
2 CONT The end was peaceful and full of hope of the better home above.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is well, it is well forever, a life comes with eternal rest.Itiswell, it is well forever,  His pl---- andwaysarebest.[062003updates.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellenburgh Depot
2 CONT
2 CONT I confirmed that Basile and Eleonore Tetreau Ashe/Dufresneisdefinitely his parents.  On the Family group it hasFrancisAshemarried Rachel Hall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne Geake  Geake-Bradley Family Roots web jgeake@qwest.net
