2 CONT Ellen BURGH DEPOT Frank Ash, aged 71, passed peacefully away Tuesday evening, July 25th, at his home in Clinton. Mr. Aash was born in Canada on Nor. 24th, 1833, and moved to Clinton Mills from Charlotte, Vt., in the fall of 18tf5.
2 CONC  He was twice married, his first wife being Rachel Hall, and to this union one child was born. His second wife was Mary Oldham, and to this" union nine child re n were born. The second wife died io the year of 1887. When Mr. Ash f
2 CONC irst located here the . ace was a dense, foreBt in^TEe settlement called " The Woods." The de ceased complained of his heart troubling him for some time before the end tame, but his Death was not looked for so soon. He was a man o
2 CONC f courage and perseverance, being able to endure great hardship, which was tne lot of the early settlers of what is called '-The Woods." He is survived by six daughters and three sous-Ida M. Hall, Montpelier, Vt.; Susette Leggett.
