1 NOTE {geni:about_me} --He was buried in St. John's Old Roman Catholic Cemetery, Plattsburgh, Clinton, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT --Jean was counted in a census on 22 July 1850 at Plattsburgh, Clinton, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT --Jean was counted in a census on 18 June 1860 at Plattsburgh, Clinton, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT --Jean was counted in a census on 01 July 1870 at Plattsburgh, Clinton, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT --Jean was counted in a census on 02 June 1880 at 48 Platt St.  Plattsburgh, Clinton, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT --Jean was counted in a census on 12 June 1900 at 60  Platt St.  Plattsburgh, Clinton, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT St. John's Old Roman Catholic Cemetery Tombstone Inscription.
2 CONT
2 CONT                  Jean B. Boisy
2 CONT
2 CONT                      Born
2 CONT
2 CONT                  Aug. 14, 1822
2 CONT
2 CONT                       Died
2 CONT
2 CONT                   Apr. 3 1900
2 CONT
2 CONT                      ~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT                     His Wife
2 CONT
2 CONT                   Marilda Proux
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1826-1909
2 CONT
2 CONT --Based on other research, I believe there is an error on the tombstone, switching the birth & dates for John and Matilda.  The 1900 Census taken in June of 1900 does not list Matilda.  The 1900 Census taken in June of 1900 does n
2 CONC ot list Matilda but it does list John as a widower.  It would seem more likely that Matilda passed away in 1900 and John in 1909
2 CONT
2 CONT
