1 NAME Dennis Henry Stanislaus /Daudelin/
2 GIVN Dennis Henry Stanislaus
2 SURN Daudelin
2 _MARNM Dolan
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 28 JAN 1845
2 PLAC Quebec, Canada
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 1902
2 PLAC Calvary Cemetery, Saint Peter, Nicollet County, Minnesota, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 FEB 1902
2 ADDR
3 CITY Mankato
3 STAE Minnesota
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dennis was a French Canadian (Dennis Henry Stanislaus DAUDELIN) who changed the spelling of his surname to "DOLAN".  
2 CONT
2 CONT Dennis died of complications of a fast growing cancer.  A large tumor had grown on his face and he was unable to eat properly.    
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Notice:
2 CONT The Saint Peter Tribune
2 CONT Wednesday February 12, 1902 
2 CONT under
2 CONT BRIEF LOCALS
2 CONT "Dennis DOLAN, of Kasota township, died from cancer of the face at the Mankato hospital on Thursday night last, where he had gone for treatment.  The funeral occurred on Saturday morning from the English Catholic church in this ci
2 CONC ty, Rev. Father Carey officiating.  His age was 60 years.  He leaves a wife and one child."
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Peter Herald
2 CONT Friday, February 14, 1902
2 CONT under 
2 CONT KASOTA DEPARTMENT
2 CONT "The funeral of Dennis DOLAN occurred last Saturday, the services being held at the English Catholic church in St. Peter, Fr. Carey officiating.  Mr. DOLAN had been afflicted over a year, and died at the hospital in Mankato.  He l
2 CONC eaves a wife and one child to mourn his loss.  In common with the public, The Herald tenders its sympathy to the bereaved family."
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: no mention is made of his first Wife Celia and their other surviving Children from that marriage in either article.  Dennis may have been estranged from his older Children.    
2 CONT
2 CONT Dennis married 1st to Celia WILLETTE on 28 June 1868 in Delavan, Faribault County, Minnesota.  They were parents of at least 6 children before Celia's untimely death on 21 July 1881 in Mankato, Blue Earth County, Minnesota.  Celia
2 CONC  had given birth to an un-named female child on 18 July 1881 who died the following day 19 July 1881.  Celia died 2 days later.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Dennis married 2nd to Elva May (twin of Ella DAVIS) DAVIS PARKER on 29 November 1890 in Mankato, Blue Earth County, Minnesota.  Elva DAVIS married 1st to Edson Charles PARKER on 15 December 1880 at Eagle Lake, Blue Earth County, M
2 CONC innesota and was mother of William Arthur PARKER born 19 July 1882.  Dennis became a step-father when he married Elva.    
2 CONT Dennis and Elva had one child togehter:  
2 CONT
2 CONT Maybelle June DOLAN born 24 November 1898.  Maybelle married Mark McDONALD.   
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Dennis DOLAN his widow Elva May DAVIS PARKER DOLAN married a 3rd time to Lester Eugene TORREY on 5 October 1905 at Kasota, Le Sueur County, Minnesota. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elva died 26 March 1939 in Minneapolis, Hennepin County, Minnesota.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/66444565/dennis-henry_stanislaus-dolan Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 Sm
2 CONC artCopy]: ''Aug 10 2022, 5:19:02 UTC''
