1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dated 11/12/42
2 CONT
2 CONT EARLY MINER HERE DIES AT MUSKEGON
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bodoh Succumbs at 83, Funeral to be conducted here.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bodoh, 83, an early resident of the Gogebic range, died last night at 9 o’clock at Muskegon where he had been making his home with a daughter, Mrs. Jesse Pellern.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body will arrive here Friday and may be viewed at the McKevitt-Kershner-Patrick Co. funeral home until the time of the services which will be held Saturday morning at 9 o’clock at St. Ambrose church, the Rev J.R. Moriarty offi
2 CONC ciating. Burial will be in the Wakefield cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Bodoh was born in New York on August 2 1859, and he came to the Gogebic range as a miner in the 1890’s, first setling at Ramsay where he lived until 1915? He moved to Hibbing and worked at the Hulrust pit for the Oliver Iron M
2 CONC ining Co. until 1933 when he retired. Mrs. Bodoh died in 1932. In 1940, he went to Muskegon to live with his daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides Mrs. Pellern, The deceased is survived by one son, John A. Bodoh of Hibbing and two other daughters, Mrs. George Sanders of Ironwood and Mrs. John H. Bodoh of Munising. Mr. Bodoh is also survived by 11 grandchildren and tw
2 CONC o great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcribed by Brian Sanders 2008.
