1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Flint Journal, The (MI) - Wednesday, April 24, 2002
2 CONT Deceased Name: LAURIN
2 CONT LAURIN, Elizabeth A. "Betty" - Of Burton, age 88, died Monday, April 22, 2002 at Genesys Hospice Care Center in Goodrich. Funeral Mass will be celebrated at 11AM Friday, April 26, 2002 at St. Luke Catholic Church, 3202 Forest Hill
2 CONC  in Flint, Father Gary L. McInnis officiating. Burial in New Calvary Catholic Cemetery. Those desiring may make contributions to Genesys Hospice Care Center. Visitation 1-4 and 6-8PM Thursday at the Swartz Funeral Home, 1225 West 
2 CONC Hill Road. A scripture service will be held at 7PM Thursday at the funeral home. Mrs. Laurin will be at the church from 10AM until the time of the Mass on Friday. She was born in Nadeau, Michigan on August 31, 1913 and was the dau
2 CONC ghter of Peter and Zuleima (Perras) Poupore. She married Wilbur Laurin on December 30, 1931. She was a member of St. Luke Catholic Church and the Altar Society. Surviving are 5 children, Janice and husband Kenneth Ayres, Carole an
2 CONC d husband Jack Bethurum, Nancy Wallace, Linda and husband Jerry Squires, John and wife Carolyn; daughter-in-law, Jean Laurin; 20 grandchildren; 23 great-grandchildren; 6 step-great-grandchildren; 2 great-great-grandchildren; siste
2 CONC r, Marie Dokken; many nieces and nephews. She was preceded in death by her husband, Wilbur, in 1995; son, Thomas; 2 daughters, Sandra Draper and Susan Laurin; 7 brothers; 4 sisters; and great-granddaughter, Amanda Siner. The Lauri
2 CONC n family would like to express a special thanks to Genesys Hospice Care Center.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/141758241/elizabeth-angeline-laurin Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy
