0 @N6000000000951157169@ NOTE Per Patricia Lafayette, Grosse Ile, MI, 8/30/99 & 10/16/99:
1 CONT
1 CONT Dominic baptized at St John the Baptist Church, Amherstburg,Ontario Canada. Dominic died in Saginaw, buried at Sacred HeartChurch Cemetery on Grosse Ile. Dominic, his wife and his nineliving children moved to Saginaw c.1878 or 187
1 CONC 9. From that timeuntil WWII there was always a lot of travel and visiting betweenGrosse Ile and the Saginaw Lafayettes. Two of Dominic'sdaughters, Marie Elizabeth "MInnie" and Marie Angelique"Angeline" came to work on Grosse Ile i
1 CONC n a summer hotel, c.1890,then married there and lived there all their lives as nearneighbors. Angeline's son related the Saginaw uncles were proudof the fact they were all self-employed and had never found itnecessary to work for 
1 CONC someone else. Their skills as trappers,hunters and fishermen allowed them to be independent their wholelives. Peter played the fiddle and the whole family loved todance, during the holidays he remembered the feast of the roastsuck
1 CONC ling pig with an apple in it's mouth. Angeline's son did notRemember his "grandfather Lafayette" who died in 1892, but knewhis grandmother as as "grandmother Couveau. She had remarriedand the grandson remembered the man as a nativ
1 CONC e American Indian.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1870 Michigan Census, roll #710, p. 245, line # 24-30:
1 CONT
1 CONT Dwelling 100, family 98, Monguagon Township, Wayne County.Dominic Lafayette, age 24, farmer, value of personal estate 760,born in Canada, cannot read or write, parents of foreign birth.Victoria, age 28, keeping house, born in Cana
1 CONC da, cannot read orwrite, parents of foreign birth.
1 CONT
1 CONT Lists: Jane V., age 13
1 CONT Dan D., age 10
1 CONT John, age 8
1 CONT Alexander age 6
1 CONT Peter J., age 3.
1 CONT
1 CONT Moved to Saginaw, circa 1878
1 CONT
1 CONT 1880 Michigan Census: Saginaw
1 CONT
1 CONT Little Street dwelling 130, family 133. First name also spelledDominick. States male, white, age 47, husband, married, work onbook, has ague, can't read or write, born in French Canada,parents born in French Canada. 
